WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.690
Hi! How does a sentence begin and end? Today we'll learn capital letters, full stops and question marks.

2
00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.266
The first letter of a sentence is a capital.

3
00:00:13.416 --> 00:00:17.610
I is always a capital, wherever it is: Mum and I.

4
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.522
Names of people and places start with a capital.

5
00:00:21.672 --> 00:00:26.130
Days and months start with capitals too.

6
00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:29.538
A telling sentence ends with a full stop.

7
00:00:29.688 --> 00:00:33.138
An asking sentence ends with a question mark.

8
00:00:33.288 --> 00:00:38.586
Sentences starting with What, Where, Who, Can or Is are often questions.

9
00:00:38.736 --> 00:00:43.890
Where is my bag? It ends with a question mark.

10
00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:48.066
Watch out! A sentence starts with a capital!

11
00:00:48.216 --> 00:00:50.634
My needs a capital M.

12
00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:55.386
Add a full stop: My dog is brown.

13
00:00:55.536 --> 00:01:03.978
Your turn! Can you swim: what goes at the end? Pause and think.

14
00:01:04.128 --> 00:01:09.570
It asks, so a question mark. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:18.330
Another one! I like rice: what goes at the end? Pause and think.

16
00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:23.754
It tells, so a full stop. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:23.904 --> 00:01:31.578
Here's another! Which one is right? Pause and think.

18
00:01:31.728 --> 00:01:37.290
It must start with a capital: We. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:45.618
Try one more! Which word needs a capital? Pause and think.

20
00:01:45.768 --> 00:01:51.714
Tom is a name, so it needs a capital. Did you get it right?

21
00:01:51.864 --> 00:02:00.714
Try one more! Who is your teacher: what goes at the end? Pause and think.

22
00:02:00.864 --> 00:02:06.690
It starts with who, so it's a question. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:14.802
Try one more! Mum and, ___, cook. Pause and think.

24
00:02:14.952 --> 00:02:20.130
I is always a capital. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:27.978
Try one more! Which one is right? Pause and think.

26
00:02:28.128 --> 00:02:33.618
Days need capitals: Monday. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:33.768 --> 00:02:42.234
Try one more! Where do you live: what goes at the end? Pause and think.

28
00:02:42.384 --> 00:02:48.329
It starts with where, so a question mark. Did you get it right?

29
00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:56.489
Last one! Which word needs a capital? Pause and think.

30
00:02:56.639 --> 00:03:02.561
May is a month, so it needs a capital. Did you get it right?

31
00:03:02.711 --> 00:03:11.801
Remember: start with a capital; I and names are capitals; telling sentences end with a full stop, questions with a question mark.

32
00:03:11.951 --> 00:03:17.489
Write one telling sentence and one question for your family!

